ath12k: ahb: subscribe to the root PD's SSR name

ath12k_ahb_register_rproc_notifier() passes rproc->name to
qcom_register_ssr_notifier(), but that function is keyed by the SSR name a
remoteproc driver registers with qcom_add_ssr_subdev(), not by the
remoteproc's own name.

For the WCSS root PD those differ. qcom_q6v5_mpd registers "q6wcss", the
same short logical name qcom_q6v5_wcss.c uses, while rproc->name is the
device tree node name -- "d100000.remoteproc" on IPQ5332. Subscribing with
the latter registers against a name nothing signals, so the root PD boots
and ath12k waits for a notification that cannot arrive:

  remoteproc remoteproc0: remote processor d100000.remoteproc is now up
  ath12k_ahb c000000.wifi: RootPD ready wait timed out
  ath12k_ahb c000000.wifi: failed to boot the remote processor Q6
  ath12k_ahb c000000.wifi: probe with driver ath12k_ahb failed with error -110

Use the SSR name instead.

Signed-off-by: Hideo Sumi <hideo.sumi@mugops.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ahb.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ahb.h
@@ -22,6 +22,11 @@
 #define ATH12K_AHB_FW_PREFIX			"q6_fw"
 #define ATH12K_AHB_FW_SUFFIX			".mdt"
 #define ATH12K_AHB_FW2				"iu_fw.mdt"
+
+/* SSR name the WCSS root PD registers with, matching qcom_q6v5_mpd's
+ * qcom_add_ssr_subdev() call.
+ */
+#define ATH12K_AHB_ROOTPD_SSR_NAME		"q6wcss"
 #define ATH12K_AHB_UPD_SWID			0x12
 
 /* Shared read-only firmware ID, mandated by the multi-PD firmware
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ahb.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ahb.c
@@ -862,7 +862,21 @@
 	ab_ahb->root_pd_nb.notifier_call = ath12k_ahb_root_pd_state_notifier;
 	init_completion(&ab_ahb->rootpd_ready);
 
-	ab_ahb->root_pd_notifier = qcom_register_ssr_notifier(ab_ahb->tgt_rproc->name,
+	/* The SSR notifier is keyed by the remoteproc's *SSR name*, which is
+	 * the short logical name the remoteproc driver passes to
+	 * qcom_add_ssr_subdev() -- "q6wcss" for the WCSS root PD, the same
+	 * way qcom_q6v5_wcss.c names it, and "mpss" for the modem. It is not
+	 * rproc->name, which is the device tree node name
+	 * ("d100000.remoteproc" here).
+	 *
+	 * Subscribing with rproc->name registers against a name nothing ever
+	 * signals, so the root PD comes up and this driver waits for a
+	 * notification that cannot arrive:
+	 *
+	 *   remoteproc remoteproc0: remote processor d100000.remoteproc is now up
+	 *   ath12k_ahb c000000.wifi: RootPD ready wait timed out
+	 */
+	ab_ahb->root_pd_notifier = qcom_register_ssr_notifier(ATH12K_AHB_ROOTPD_SSR_NAME,
 							      &ab_ahb->root_pd_nb);
 	if (IS_ERR(ab_ahb->root_pd_notifier))
 		return PTR_ERR(ab_ahb->root_pd_notifier);
